```json
{
  "calls": [
    {
      "tool": "tracker.create",
      "args": {
        "title": "webhook retries exhausted",
        "severity": "S2",
        "component": "gateway",
        "assignee": "omar",
        "due_date": "2026-08-26"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "mail.send",
      "args": {
        "to": ["support@corp.example"],
        "cc": [],
        "subject": "webhook retries exhausted S2",
        "body": "{{call_1.ticket_id}}",
        "priority": "high"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Notes:
- `due_date`: "Wednesday" resolved against header date 2026-08-24 (Monday) → **2026-08-26**.
- Ordering matters: `tracker.create` must execute before `mail.send`, because the email body must reference the ticket id.
- `body`: the source specifies only that the body must reference the ticket id; no other body content is given, so the body is emitted as a runtime binding (`{{call_1.ticket_id}}`) to the ticket id returned by call 1 rather than fabricated prose.
- `cc` is empty (no cc stated in source); `priority` is "high" as explicitly stated.
